_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 24
---
order: 24
---
short_label: V.24
---
statement: If a first magnitude has to a second the same ratio as a third has to a fourth, and also a fifth has to the second the same ratio as a sixth to the fourth, then the sum of the first and fifth has to the second the same ratio as the sum of the third and sixth has to the fourth.
---
proof:

Let a first magnitude *AB* have to a second *C* the same ratio as a third *DE* has to a fourth *F,* and let also a fifth *BG* have to the second *C* the same ratio as a sixth *EH* has to the fourth *F.*

I say that the sum of the first and fifth, *AG,* has to the second *C* the same ratio as the sum of the third and sixth, *DH,* has to the fourth *F.*

<figure class="diagram">
